{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01AVR2YX7P8Gf9CQQTkzhc6L","type":"tool_result","content":"=== Cargo.toml ===\n[package]\nname = \"translation\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2021\"\n\n[lib]\nname = \"gaussian_kernel_lib\"\ncrate-type = [\"cdylib\"]\npath = \"src/lib.rs\"\n\n[profile.release]\npanic = \"abort\"\n\n[workspace]\n=== Cargo.lock ===\n# This file is automatically @generated by Cargo.\n# It is not intended for manual editing.\nversion = 4\n\n[[package]]\nname = \"translation\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\n=== src/lib.rs ===\n     1\t//! Rust translation of the C library in `c_src/`.\n     2\t//!\n     3\t//! Public ABI (matches `nm -D` on the C shared library exactly):\n     4\t//!   * `gaussian_kernel`\n     5\t//!\n     6\t//! Original C source (`c_src/src/lib.c`):\n     7\t//!\n     8\t//! ```c\n     9\t//! void gaussian_kernel(float *dest, int size, float radius) {\n    10\t//!     float *k;\n    11\t//!     float rs, s2, sum;\n    12\t//!     float sigma = 1.6f;\n    13\t//!     float tetha = 2.25f;\n    14\t//!     int r, hsize = size / 2;\n    15\t//!     s2 = 1.0f / expf(sigma * sigma * tetha);\n    16\t//!     rs = sigma / radius;\n    17\t//!     k = dest;\n    18\t//!     sum = 0.0f;\n    19\t//!     for (r = -hsize; r <= hsize; r++) {\n    20\t//!         float x = r * rs;\n    21\t//!         float v = (1.0f / expf(x * x)) - s2;\n    22\t//!         v = (((v) > (0)) ? (v) : (0));\n    23\t//!         *k = v;\n    24\t//!         sum += v;\n    25\t//!         k++;\n    26\t//!     }\n    27\t//!     if (sum > 0.0f) {\n    28\t//!         float isum = 1.0f / sum;\n    29\t//!         for (r = 0; r < size; r++)\n    30\t//!             dest[r] *= isum;\n    31\t//!     }\n    32\t//! }\n    33\t//! ```\n    34\t//!\n    35\t//! Behavioural notes (bugs are preserved verbatim, not fixed):\n    36\t//!   * `hsize = size / 2` uses C integer division (truncation toward zero), and\n    37\t//!     the kernel loop runs over the inclusive range `[-hsize, hsize]`, i.e.\n    38\t//!     `2 * hsize + 1` iterations. For an even `size` this writes `size + 1`\n    39\t//!     floats into `dest` -- one element past what the caller's `size` implies.\n    40\t//!     That out-of-bounds store is part of the observable C behaviour and is\n    41\t//!     reproduced here.\n    42\t//!   * For a negative `size`, `-hsize > hsize`, so the loop body never runs,\n    43\t//!     `sum` stays `0.0` and nothing is written or normalised.\n    44\t//!   * `radius == 0.0` yields `rs == inf`; `x * x` is then `inf` (or `NaN` when\n    45\t//!     `r == 0`, since `0 * inf == NaN`), matching the C exactly.\n    46\t//!   * The clamp `v > 0 ? v : 0` compares against `0` promoted to `0.0f`, so a\n    47\t//!     `NaN` `v` fails the comparison and becomes `+0.0f`.\n    48\t\n    49\t#![allow(non_snake_case)]\n    50\t\n    51\tuse std::ffi::c_int;\n    52\t\n    53\textern \"C\" {\n    54\t    /// The very same `expf` from the platform libm that the C build links\n    55\t    /// against (`target_link_libraries(... m)`), so the results are\n    56\t    /// bit-for-bit identical instead of merely close.\n    57\t    fn expf(x: f32) -> f32;\n    58\t}\n    59\t\n    60\t/// Fill `dest` with a normalised, pedestal-subtracted Gaussian kernel.\n    61\t///\n    62\t/// # Safety\n    63\t///\n    64\t/// `dest` must be valid for writes of `2 * (size / 2) + 1` `f32` values (note\n    65\t/// that this is `size + 1` when `size` is even -- see the module docs) and must\n    66\t/// be valid for reads and writes of `size` `f32` values. Exactly the contract\n    67\t/// the C function imposes on its callers.\n    68\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n    69\tpub unsafe extern \"C\" fn gaussian_kernel(dest: *mut f32, size: c_int, radius: f32) {\n    70\t    let sigma: f32 = 1.6f32;\n    71\t    let tetha: f32 = 2.25f32;\n    72\t    let hsize: c_int = size / 2;\n    73\t\n    74\t    let s2: f32 = 1.0f32 / expf(sigma * sigma