NF` — `rs = +0`, every tap `V0`, normalised (even `size` ⇒ `1/(size+1)`) | [x] |\n| C12 | `gaussian_kernel` | mixed sizes × `R_NEG_INF` — `rs = -0.0` | [x] |\n| C13 | `gaussian_kernel` | mixed sizes × `R_POS_ZERO` — `rs = +inf`, `sum == 0`, normalisation skipped | [x] |\n| C14 | `gaussian_kernel` | mixed sizes × `R_NEG_ZERO` — `rs = -inf` | [x] |\n| C15 | `gaussian_kernel` | mixed sizes × `R_NAN` (8 distinct NaN bit patterns incl. sNaN and sign-set) | [x] |\n| C16 | `gaussian_kernel` | mixed sizes × `R_SUBNORMAL` (incl. `0x00000001`, `0x007fffff`, negatives) — `rs` overflows to `±inf` | [x] |\n| C17 | `gaussian_kernel` | `S_ZERO` × all `R` classes — one unnormalised store | [x] |\n| C18 | `gaussian_kernel` | `S_NEG_ONE` × all `R` classes — one unnormalised store (truncation toward zero) | [x] |\n| C19 | `gaussian_kernel` | `S_NEG` (random in `-2..=-100000`) × all `R` classes × `F_RANDOM` — zero stores, buffer untouched | [x] |\n| C20 | `gaussian_kernel` | `S_INT_MIN` × all `R` classes — zero stores, no negation overflow | [x] |\n| C21 | `gaussian_kernel` | `S_NEG` × `P_NULL` — the only null-pointer configuration the C tolerates | [x] |\n| C22 | `gaussian_kernel` | all size classes × `R_TYPICAL` × `P_OFFSET` (offsets 1, 3, 7) — no base-alignment assumption | [x] |\n| C23 | `gaussian_kernel` | all size classes × `R_TYPICAL` × `F_ZERO` and `F_RANDOM` — pre-existing contents must not leak into the result (and must survive where the C does not store) | [x] |\n| C24 | `gaussian_kernel` | back-to-back invocation: same buffer called twice with different `(size, radius)` — verifies there is no hidden state and that the second call's partial overwrite matches | [x] |\n| C25 | `gaussian_kernel` | full fuzz: `size` uniform in `-8..=64` × `R_RANDOM_BITS` (any 32-bit pattern) × random fill × random pointer offset, 20 000 draws | [x] |\n| C26 | `gaussian_kernel` | full fuzz, large: `size` uniform in `1..=2048` × `R_RANDOM_BITS`, 2 000 draws | [x] |\n| C27 | `gaussian_kernel` | exh