{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_2aq4fnd3ysdg2m4d5eut33vwqlpnfjfspq6carg235zv42enjgpq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src` is a single 28-line function, `void gaussian_kernel(float *dest, int size, float radius)` — a normalized, pedestal-subtracted Gaussian kernel generator with `sigma = 1.6f`, `tetha = 2.25f`.\n\n## Phase A — surface mapped (3 artifacts in `translation/`)\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — `nm -D --defined-only` is *exactly* `T gaussian_kernel` on both `.so`s. Diff empty; nothing untranslated (CMake compiles one TU; grep confirms no other functions/statics/macros/types), nothing stubbed.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — grep proved the C has **0** `return`s, asserts, null checks, error enums/macros, `#ifdef`s — just one `if` and one ternary. So the rejection surface is entirely *implicit*, documented as 18 rows + 6 generic FFI-boundary rows.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 29 rows from the cross-product of the axes the C actually branches on: `size` shape (odd/even/1/0/−1/≤−2/`INT_MIN`), `radius` class (typical/wide/narrow/threshold/negative/±0/±inf/NaN/subnormal/random bits), buffer pre-fill, and pointer offset.\n\n## Phases B–D — results\n\nAll 55 tests green across all 4 configurations (`default` / `--no-default-features` × `debug` / `release`), driven by `translation/run_all_tests.sh`. **73,407** differential comparisons, each comparing the *whole* buffer bit-for-bit (bytes before `dest`, payload, the slot the C overruns, and 16 `f32` of guard) — so 1-ULP divergences, wrong store *counts*, NaN payloads and zero signs all fail.\n\nBoth `.so`s are loaded via `libloading`; Rust is only ever reached through its exported symbol.\n\n## Key C quirks confirmed preserved (not \"fixed\")\n\n1. `hsize = size/2` with an inclusive `[-hsize, hsize]` loop writes **`size+1`** floats for even `size` — a 4-byte overrun, and that last store is never normalized.\n2. `size == 0` and `size == -1` both store one **unnormalized** element (C truncation: `-1/2 == 0`).\n3. `size <= -2` stores *nothing* — the only case where `NULL dest` is safe.\n4. `radius == ±0` / NaN / tiny subnormal ⇒ every tap clamps to `+0.0f`, `sum == 0`, normalization skipped. A NaN is never stored (`NaN > 0` is false).\n5. `radius == ±inf` ⇒ `rs == ±0` ⇒ flat kernel.\n\nBit-exactness is attainable because `objdump` shows GCC does **not** constant-fold `expf(sigma*sigma*tetha)` at the default CMake build type — both libraries call the same glibc `expf@GLIBC_2.27`.\n\n## Harness validated by mutation testing\n\nI injected 26 deliberate bugs one at a time. All 16 non-equivalent mutants were **killed** (wrong division semantics, loop off-by-ones, clamp-to-`-0.0`, `sum >= 0`, constant typos, `expf(-x)` vs `1/expf(x)`, reciprocal-multiply). The 10 survivors are each *proven* semantically identical (e.g. `|x|*|x| == x*x`; exact `f64` intermediates round identically; `(s*s)*t` and `s*(s*t)` both give `0x40b851ec`), so surviving is correct rather than a coverage hole.\n\nI made no changes to `c_src/` (checksums recorded) and the only change to the Rust source was reverting my own mutation-test scratch edits — **the translation needed no correctness fixes**. I added `libloading` to `[dev-dependencies]`, the three Phase A artifacts, `VERIFICATION.md`, `run_all_tests.sh`, and four test files."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1295,"cache_read_input_tokens":166827,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1295,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17cfe536-164f-4671-b86d-ad805376921c","uuid":"8157ec23-75a2-4195-ace5-34fb09a18eef","timestamp":"2026-08-26T21:50:40.334Z"}
